Every file under this directory that is rlxfw's own -- that is, every file here
with no imported source and no IMPORTED marker -- is licensed GPL-2.0-only.
That is forced by provenance and is not a choice: these files are compiled into,
and linked with, a kernel whose own COPYING says version 2 and not "or later".
`NOTICE` section 2 carries the reading and the measurement behind it.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS INSTEAD OF A PER-FILE SPDX LINE AT THE TOP.
量 2026-10-04 over `git ls-files '*.md'`: the twelve basenames under this
directory are cited BY LINE NUMBER 213 times, 115 of them distinct, and 108 of
those citing lines are in 15 files that `tools/citecheck.py` reads.  An
`SPDX-License-Identifier` inserted as line 1 of those files shifts every line
by one and rots all 108 at once, and `tools/spec-check.py`'s C11 token-checks
the same population by basename, so both checkers would go red.  The remaining
105 of the 213 are in LOG.md and in frozen bench/ cards, which resolve against
the file as it was at their own commit and must not be renumbered at all.

So the statement is here, where it moves no line.  A per-file comment at the
END of each file would work equally well and is the alternative that was not
taken, because one file naming the directory is one place to keep correct.

WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT ESTABLISH.
Which files here are rlxfw's own: `docs/sbom.md` owns the component list and
`docs/vendor-modifications.md` names the vendor files rlxfw changes.  Where
this file and either of those disagree, they own the fact and this file is
wrong.  It is also not legal advice; `NOTICE` says the same and says why.
